    "symmetry_note": "CONVENTION D (2026-08-26). This field used to read: 'Every negative-norm forbidden block is the conjugate lambda -> lambda' of a dominant positive block with tr_M(P_lambda) sign-flipped -- the S7b bar-involution / Type-B-folding signature.' That was a convention-C statement and it does not survive: under D there are NO negative-norm blocks, so sign_flip_conjugate_pairs is empty and the claimed signature has no instances. What conjugation does under D is map the entire support (the two-row partitions) into the kernel, since a two-row lambda of n >= 6 has lambda_1 >= 3 hence ell(lambda') >= 3. (3,2,1) remains the self-conjugate partition of 6, and under D its weight is zero -- it sits in the kernel, not at a fixed point of a sign flip.",
